# Neo Analyzer parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoAnalyzer
namespace NeoBuzz.Analyzer
class NeoAnalyzerMachine
summary Analyzer that passes audio through untouched and shows its spectrum (FFT with peak hold, third-octave bars), loudness (momentary, short-term and integrated LUFS, loudness range, true peak) and stereo image (correlation, width, goniometer). Use it anywhere in a chain to watch a signal; machine_readings returns its numbers, which are the analysis library's (analyze measures the same way).

group Spectrum
Smoothing   "Smoothing"   0 3    2    enum 1/24_oct 1/12_oct 1/6_oct 1/3_oct   | Width of the band each point of the spectrum curve sums: narrow resolves single tones; 1/3 oct draws through the third-octave bars
    how Sets how wide a slice of the spectrum each point of the curve adds up, from 1/24 octave (fine) to 1/3 octave (broad).
    sound Fine settings show single tones and harmonics as sharp spikes; broad ones draw a smooth curve that reads as overall tonal balance.
Speed       "Speed"       0 3    1    enum Fast Medium Slow Very_slow          | How fast the spectrum follows the signal: averaging over about 0.1, 0.3, 1 or 3 s
    how Sets how long the spectrum averages the signal: about 0.1, 0.3, 1 or 3 seconds.
    sound Fast follows every note and hit; slow settles into a steady picture of the track's average tone.
Hold        "Peak hold"   0 1000 475  time 0.25 20                             | How long peaks hold before they fall: the spectrum's peak curve and bars, and the true-peak marker
    how Sets how long the peak curve, the bars and the true-peak marker stay up before they fall, from 0.25 to 20 seconds.
    sound The audio does not change; short holds follow the music, long ones keep the loudest moments on screen.
Tilt        "Tilt"        0 2    0    enum 0_dB/oct 3_dB/oct 4.5_dB/oct        | Display slope around 1 kHz (the readings never tilt): 0 shows pink noise flat, 3 shows a typical finished mix about flat, 4.5 leans brighter
    how Tilts the displayed spectrum around 1 kHz by 0, 3 or 4.5 dB per octave, without touching the audio or the readings.
    sound At 3 dB per octave a typical finished mix looks about flat, which makes its balance easier to judge by eye.
group Loudness
Target      "Target"      0 360  220  db -36 0                                 | The loudness (LUFS, written in dB) the meters are coloured against: −14 for streaming, −23 for broadcast
    how Sets the loudness in LUFS that the meters are coloured against, from -36 to 0; -14 suits streaming, -23 broadcast.
    sound The audio does not change; the meters show how far the track sits above or below the target.
Reset       "Reset"       0 1    0    switch                                   | On: the integrated loudness, loudness range, maxima and held peaks start again. Turn it Off, then On, for the next reset
    how Switching it on restarts the integrated loudness, the loudness range, the maxima and the held peaks.
    sound The audio does not change; the long-term figures start counting again from zero.

# What the analyzer measures (NeoAnalyzerMachine.Readings, machine_readings). Windows end now.
reading momentary_lufs        LUFS  | Loudness of the last 400 ms (BS.1770 momentary)
reading short_term_lufs       LUFS  | Loudness of the last 3 s (short-term)
reading integrated_lufs       LUFS  | Gated integrated loudness since the reset (BS.1770)
reading range_lu              LU    | Loudness range since the reset (EBU Tech 3342)
reading true_peak_dbtp        dBTP  | The highest true peak since the reset (4× oversampled, BS.1770 Annex 2)
reading momentary_max_lufs    LUFS  | The loudest 400 ms since the reset
reading short_term_max_lufs   LUFS  | The loudest 3 s since the reset
reading seconds               s     | Time measured since the reset
reading correlation           ratio | Correlation of left and right over the last 3 s: 1 mono, 0 unrelated, −1 opposed
reading width                 ratio | Side over mid energy over the last 3 s: 0 mono, 1 unrelated channels, above 1 when they oppose
reading sub_db                dB    | Level of 20–60 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (a full-scale sine reads −3 dB)
reading low_db                dB    | Level of 60–250 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading low_mid_db            dB    | Level of 250–500 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading mid_db                dB    | Level of 500 Hz – 2 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading high_mid_db           dB    | Level of 2–4 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading presence_db           dB    | Level of 4–6 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading air_db                dB    | Level of 6–20 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading band_20hz_db          dB    | Third octave at 20 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_25hz_db          dB    | Third octave at 25 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_31_5hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 31.5 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_40hz_db          dB    | Third octave at 40 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_50hz_db          dB    | Third octave at 50 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_63hz_db          dB    | Third octave at 63 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_80hz_db          dB    | Third octave at 80 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_100hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 100 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_125hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 125 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_160hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 160 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_200hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 200 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_250hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 250 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_315hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 315 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_400hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 400 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_500hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 500 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_630hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 630 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_800hz_db         dB    | Third octave at 800 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_1000hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 1 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_1250hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 1.25 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_1600hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 1.6 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_2000hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 2 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_2500hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 2.5 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_3150hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 3.15 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_4000hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 4 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_5000hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 5 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_6300hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 6.3 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_8000hz_db        dB    | Third octave at 8 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_10000hz_db       dB    | Third octave at 10 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_12500hz_db       dB    | Third octave at 12.5 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_16000hz_db       dB    | Third octave at 16 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
reading band_20000hz_db       dB    | Third octave at 20 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (ISO 266 nominal centre)
